Module censer "Censer Hill — client study" {
  Description "A short interface study in the Serewater March. The complete region and dungeon are proposed; this fixture tests only travel, conversation, combat, persistent rewards and recovery.".
  Entity party: group "The Wayfarers". Entity gold: good "Coin". Entity rations: good "Ration".
  Entity clock: clock "Time".
  Entity town: place "Reedwake · Ferry square". Entity road: place "The willow causeway".
  Entity entry: place "Censer Hill · The receiving hall". Entity crypt: place "The lower ossuary".
  Entity stair: place "The broken singers' stair".
  Person vesper "Vesper" at town { Role "ferry clerk and burial trustee". Race human. Class commoner. }
  Person oren "Oren" at entry { Role "surveyor waiting for a safe escort". Race dwarf. Class fighter. Level 2. }
  Person guardian "The White Hound" at crypt { Role "cold-altered burial guardian". Race frost_wolf. Class rime_beast. Level 2. }
  Entity seal: reward "a one-use ember seal".
  Initially Assert at(party, town). Initially Assert restful(town).
  Initially Assert route(town, road). Initially Assert route(road, town).
  Initially Assert route(road, entry). Initially Assert route(entry, road).
  Initially Assert route(entry, stair). Initially Assert route(stair, entry).
  Initially Assert route(stair, crypt). Initially Assert route(crypt, stair).
  Initially Assert at(seal, crypt). Initially Assert giftEffect(seal, cinder_lesson).
  Initially Assert rewardFor(seal, hearth). Initially Assert offeredAt(seal, crypt).
  Discovery hearth "The ember seal is a foundry lesson: one companion can learn its fire invocation permanently. Its origin does not grant ownership of the burials." {
    Known by oren.
    Source rubbing "The seal's firing instructions" at crypt readable by party.
  }
  Topic vesper_work with vesper "Why are people going to Censer Hill?" when true {
    Says "'The flood broke the ferry chain. The foundry has bronze enough for a new one, but those are our families' burial galleries now. My brother went with the salvagers. I need him back; I will not buy a bridge with stolen bones. Speak to Oren before you decide what to take.'".
  }
  Topic vesper_help with vesper "What can we prepare here?" when true {
    Says "'The inn has beds and your company has provisions. Rest here costs a ration and six hours. A cleric can heal wounds on the road. You will need to choose how far to go before turning back. Ask what the people up there claim before deciding what is yours to take.'".
  }
  Topic oren_burials with oren "What happened to the expedition?" when true {
    Says "'We split over the bronze. The others went farther down. The hound guards the lower gallery: fire can hurt it, cold scarcely does, and its howl can stun. You can turn back. There is also an old lesson seal below; taking that does not mend the ferry or recover my companions.' Oren folds his survey. 'I can tell you what I saw. I cannot promise what lies beyond.'".
  }
  Observe square at town when true "Rain ticks on the ferry office roof. Beyond the landing, a broken chain hangs in the brown water. Vesper keeps a list of the people who went up to Censer Hill. Willow country rises west of the last houses.".
  Observe willows at road when true "Willow roots grip the raised stone path. Reed warblers call from last year's stems. Above the flood line stands the old foundry: a long roof, an empty bell-frame, and a dark receiving door. You can continue or return before committing supplies.".
  Observe hall at entry when true "Someone has swept a dry square among the fallen plaster. Oren sits beside a measuring staff. The broad passage descends toward the singers' stair. Light from the doorway remains at your back.".
  Observe steps at stair when true "Worn steps turn beneath a row of empty niches. A cold draught rises from the lower ossuary. Water has left a pale line across the lowest step. The air smells of limestone and old charcoal.".
  Observe hound at crypt when able(guardian) "The White Hound stands between chalk burial slabs. Cold has bleached its coat. Its rime bite can weaken; its howl can stun. A small ember seal rests in a side niche, beside its firing instructions. The hound watches the burial slabs. The stair remains behind you.".
  Observe remains at crypt when dead(guardian) "The White Hound lies still. The crypt does not reset: the injuries and death are part of this campaign. The burial slabs remain undisturbed. The ember seal can be read and accepted if it is still here.".
  Observe taken at crypt when claimed(seal) "The seal has crumbled. Its invocation belongs to the companion who learned it, and will remain available in future encounters. Return to Reedwake to recover; nothing ends the campaign here.".
  Goal false.
}
